# Preserve shipping versions

Shipping releases are immutable. Versions exist so a known-good ship stays recoverable.

## N-2 rolling window + golden

Keep the **last two** recoverable ships (**N** and **N-1**) plus Drive golden forever. See [docs/RESTORE.md](docs/RESTORE.md).

Current slots (do not delete tags or `out/` ISO dirs when cutting the next ship):

- **Golden (forever):** `v0.2.0` / Drive ISO / `checksums/v0.2.sha256`
- **N-1:** `v0.3.8` / Drive + `out/v0.3.8/` / `checksums/v0.3.8.sha256` (`88f78154…`)
- **N:** `v0.3.9` / Drive + `out/v0.3.9/` / `checksums/v0.3.9.sha256` (`32a37a66…`)

**Do not flash `v0.3.5`** (truncated ISO). Prefer **v0.3.9**. `v0.3.6` stays published; do not delete or overwrite it.

## Never overwrite

- Do **not** move, retag, delete, or force-rewrite tag `v0.2.0`, `v0.2.1-local-nvidia-kbd`, `v0.3.0`, `v0.3.6`, `v0.3.8`, `v0.3.9`, or any published shipping tag.
- Do **not** change or replace published checksum files once shipped.
- Do **not** overwrite the Drive / StickLLM-releases **v0.2** ISO artifact (hash `4914087d…`).
- Do **not** overwrite the Drive **v0.3.6** ISO under the same name if contents differ (hash `fb559d9f…`).
- Do **not** overwrite the Drive **v0.3.8** ISO under the same name if contents differ (hash `88f78154…`).
- Do **not** overwrite the Drive **v0.3.9** ISO under the same name if contents differ (hash `32a37a66…`).
- Do **not** flash or publish a later build under an existing release name if contents differ.
- When cutting **v0.4+**, do **not** delete N/N-1 tags or their `out/<version>/` ISO directories.

## New work gets new names

- New product work → new tag (`v0.4.0`, `v0.3.9`, …), new `out/<version>/StickLLM-vX.Y.Z.iso`, new checksum file.
- **Naming:** v0.3.7+ use exactly `StickLLM-vX.Y.Z.iso` (example: `StickLLM-v0.3.8.iso`). Through v0.3.6, published files stay `stickllm-amd-rtx3090-v….hybrid.iso` — never rename or rewrite those.
- Rebuilds of an older line → distinct `out/` path; never overwrite a shipping ISO name. Compare hash to the shipping checksum; report bit-identical if equal.
- WIP / abandoned experiments → branch only (`wip/…`); never replace a shipping tag or Drive ISO.

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD: build v0.4 and delete out/v0.3.8/ or tag -d v0.3.8
❌ BAD: build v0.3 and write over out/stickllm-amd-rtx3090.hybrid.iso (the v0.2 Drive ship)
❌ BAD: git tag -f v0.2.0 <new-commit>
❌ BAD: edit checksums/v0.2.sha256 to match a different ISO
❌ BAD: rename stickllm-amd-rtx3090-v0.3.6.hybrid.iso to StickLLM-v0.3.6.iso

✅ GOOD: out/v0.3.6/stickllm-amd-rtx3090-v0.3.6.hybrid.iso + checksums/v0.3.6.sha256 (N-1; leave as-is)
✅ GOOD: out/v0.3.8/StickLLM-v0.3.8.iso + checksums/v0.3.8.sha256 + tag v0.3.8 (N-1; leave as-is)
✅ GOOD: out/v0.3.9/StickLLM-v0.3.9.iso + checksums/v0.3.9.sha256 + tag v0.3.9
✅ GOOD: out/v0.4.0/StickLLM-v0.4.0.iso + checksums/v0.4.0.sha256 + tag v0.4.0 (keep prior N/N-1)
```
